    id: 'mon-105',
    title: '\'Balatro\' Community Playbook: From Launch to Letting Go',
    description: 'How do you build a thriving game community, then step back and let it run itself? In this session, Emma Smith-Bodie, Community Manager at Playstack, shares how indie hit Balatro cultivated a self-sustaining player community on Discord and Reddit. From creating the right foundations to knowing when to let go, she\'ll walk through practical tactics for attracting early players, maintaining long-term engagement, and handing over the reins to your fans. Learn how to foster loyalty, spark genuine conversation, and recognize when your players are ready to lead. You will leave with actionable strategies and a new perspective on community building, one where stepping back is the ultimate sign of success.',
