    description: 'The games industry is entering a period of rapid change, and AI is reshaping both sides of the fight against cheating. Cheat developers are already using AI to mimic human behavior, mask suspicious patterns, and automate entire cheat operations at scale. In response, studios and security partners are deploying AI-driven systems to detect non-human and unfair play faster, earlier, and with greater precision. This session explores how AI is redefining the battle for fair play, what the next generation of cheating threats is likely to look like, and how studios can stay ahead of them without resorting to intrusive systems that undermine player trust or experience.',
