    description: 'At GDC 2011, Stone spoke about 15 tabletop games he created for his family and close friends. 15 years later, he has continued this tradition of designing a new game every year: a play-by-mail game for his sons in college, a real-time rhythm card game for drum students, a social game for a wedding, and—most recently—several highly personalized tabletop games for his four grandchildren. In this session, Stone details those 15 games and describes how his design philosophy evolved during that time. Each game teaches its own special lesson, with unique constraints shaped by the experiences of his small audience. Many of the tips and techniques can be applied to games that you create for the people closest in your life.',
