    description: 'Games have become the modern world\'s social commons, where friendships form, conflicts play out, and culture is created in real time. This panel brings together community designers, trust & safety leads, and game directors to explore practical strategies for how studios can nurture positive community behavior and transform toxicity into teachable moments. Panelists will share:  Moderation frameworks that scale from indie to AAA  Design interventions that reward pro-social behavior without feeling heavy-handed  Player education systems that shift mindsets rather than simply punishing actions  Case studies from studios that transformed repeat offenders into positive community leaders through targeted intervention Through data-driven insights and lived experience, the panel will demonstrate how empathy- driven design, transparent communication, and systemic thinking can build resilient communities that self-regulate and thrive.',
