    title: 'The Invisible Layer: Redesigning Communication and Navigation in \'Candy Crush Soda Saga\'',
    description: 'In live games, it\'s often not the feature itself that fails - it\'s how players find it, understand it, and choose to engage with it. This session shares how King\'s Candy Crush Soda Saga is strategically redesigning its Communication & Navigation systems after a decade of feature sprawl, UX debt, and scattered entry points. It\'s a candid look at system-level transformation on a live game played by millions: one that required cross-discipline alignment, buy-in to address invisible friction, and the willingness to challenge legacy assumptions. The talk explores how Communication & Navigation is becoming a foundation for improvements in gameplay clarity, personalization, and scalability. For anyone evolving a live game without starting from scratch, this session offers a blueprint for redesigning the layer players rarely notice, but always feel.',
