    title: 'When East Meets Western: Art Direction of \'Ghost of Yōtei\'',
    description: 'Ghost of Yōtei blends the vibe of classic Westerns with that of Japanese samurai movies. That means long sightlines over vast, empty areas. Authentic Japanese visuals, but recast from the close quarters of Tsushima to the openness and incredible scale of Hokkaido, the frontier of Japan when the game takes place. Sometimes even a feeling of loneliness, alone with a sword and a horse with nobody in sight for miles in any direction. Art Director Joanna Wang walks through how the team went from this statement of purpose to the beautiful, fully realized world of Ghost of Yōtei. She covers the definition and discovery of the key focus areas that created our target vibe and follows up with the production process the team used to deliver on the emotional promise of the game.',
