    title: 'Expanding Globally: How Alternative Payment Methods Unlock International Player Growth (Presented by Antom)',
    description: 'This session explores how payment strategy directly impacts global player acquisition and monetization for game publishers. As games scale beyond their home markets, understanding regional payment preferences becomes critical to reaching new audiences and reducing conversion friction. The session also briefly introduces Antom, a leading global payment provider connecting businesses to over 2.2 billion users worldwide. It highlights key payment trends across major gaming markets, including the rise of digital wallets and alternative payment methods preferred by players in emerging regions. Through real-world case studies, attendees will learn how game publishers leverage localized payment experiences to improve checkout conversion, expand into new markets, and accelerate international growth. The session provides practical insights into building a payment strategy that supports long-term global expansion.',
