    id: 'thu-020',
    title: 'Getting the Ball Rolling: Advancing Game Accessibility Through Interactive Workshops',
    description: 'Learn by doing. Work with other attendees to design a game accessibility workshop from scratch. Workshops like these are the cornerstone of culture and process changes throughout the industry. This hands-on walkthrough, hosted by two game accessibility workshop experts, Anna Waismeyer from Xbox and Cari Watterton from Scopely, covers the content, structure, and logistics behind an impactful accessibility workshop experience. Workshop Part 1: 10:30am – 12 pm (1.5 hr) 10:30 – 10:50am Introduction 10:50 – 11:20am Inclusive Design Foundations 11:20 – 12:00pm Accessibility Workshops Overview and Q&A LUNCH: 12:00 – 1:30pm (1.5 hr) Workshop Part 2: 1:30 – 3:30 pm (2.0 hr) 1:30 - 2:00pm Welcome back and Worksheet Overview 2:00 - 3:30pm Workshop Planning and Creation',
