    title: 'Canceled: Designing Content Creator Campaigns That Don\'t Burn Out at Launch',
    description: 'In this session, Lurkit\'s CMXO breaks down how to build and execute full-lifecycle content creator strategies that drive sustained success across pre-launch, launch, and post-launch phases. Using Dune: Awakening, Clair Obscur: Expedition 33, and Ready or Not (Console) as case studies, the talk showcases how Lurkit deconstructs games to identify the right creator archetypes and audiences—sometimes uncovering surprising fits, like the synergy between DayZ creators and Dune. Attendees will learn how to negotiate, onboard, and manage both organic and paid creators, ensure high compliance and engagement, and prevent campaign pitfalls like gray market reselling or inflated viewership. The talk also covers how to use creator programs and scalable missions to maintain long-term buzz post-launch. This is a hands-on, practical look at what makes creator campaigns work—and how to build creator pipelines that last.',
